Pittsburgh Penguins 4-3 on Thursday night.","story":"PITTSBURGH -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080143/logan-cooley\">Logan Cooley</a> completed a hat trick against his hometown team with a second left, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024868/mikhail-sergachev\">Mikhail Sergachev</a> scored at 3:27 of overtime and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/utah/utah-mammoth\">Utah Mammoth</a> stunned the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-penguins\">Pittsburgh Penguins</a> 4-3 on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              After <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291947/ben-kindel\">Ben Kindel</a> put Pittsburgh ahead 3-2 with 25 seconds left, Cooley — playing his third NHL game in Pittsburgh — batted the puck in from the left side of the net for sixth goal in four games and seventh of the season.\n\n\r\n              Cooley became the third Pittsburgh native with a hat trick against the Penguins, joining Brandon Saad and R.J. Umberger. At age 5, Cooley took part in Sidney Crosby’s first Little Penguins Learn to Play Hockey program.\n\n\r\n              Cooley scored for the first time in seven games against Pittsburgh. He had two first-period goals to give the Mammoth an early 2-0 lead, and scored in the third for his third career hat trick.\n\n\r\n              In overtime, Sergachev beat <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4576894/arturs-silovs\">Arturs Silovs</a> off a rebound in front.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874732/sebastian-cossa\">Sebastian Cossa</a> stopped 31 shots for the Mammoth, who have won three of their last five games overall. Utah is 5-0-0 after a loss and 8-0-0 when leading after two periods.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562629/rickard-rakell\">Rickard Rakell</a> had a short-handed goal, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5164/erik-karlsson\">Erik Karlsson</a> also scored for Pittsburgh. Silovs made 30 saves.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              <hl2 />\r\n              Mammoth: At Philadelphia on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              Penguins: At Montreal on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              AP NHL: <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">https://apnews.com/hub/nhl</a>","published":"2026-10-30T02:15:46Z"}}